      "name": "week_quota_future_dated_session_drift",
      "description": "KNOWN DRIFT (see the task report, not fixed here): /api/sessions/history has no upper date bound (SessionsController.GetHistory: `StartTime >= from` only), so it can return sessions scheduled arbitrarily far in the future. The real C# app (Index.razor.cs) bounds its week-sessions filter to `StartTime.Date >= weekStart && < weekStart.AddDays(7)`, correctly excluding a session almost 4 weeks out. coordinator.py's week_sessions/week_hours filter (`s.start.date() >= week_start`, coordinator.py) has NO upper bound at all, so it wrongly includes that future session's hours in 'this week'. Expected values below are the CORRECT (bounded) C# truth (weekHours=2.0, only the 2026-01-06 session) - the HA coordinator is expected to compute weekHours=6.0 (2+4) instead, which is the drift this scenario exists to surface, not paper over.",
